 "observations": [
  "The page number «123» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 12», in bold sans serif, underlined. The titles (L01, L02), in bold, the sigla and the note number in roman: L01 that of C and O, L02 that of C and N; the folios of the manuscripts, «C 49v—50r, O 106r,» over «N 29r.», stand at the left of the titles, the letters raised; here as left margin notes, divided after «C 49v—50r,» so that they keep within the page. At the foot, the signature «16*» on the right.",
  "The table: a thick and a thin rule above the head, a double rule below it; vertical rules divide the fifteen columns, double ones before and after each column of arguments; thin rules under the heads that span the four columns of signs, degrees, minutes and seconds, whose heads «Sig.», «Gr.», «Min.», «Sec.» are set in small bold type, only the first «Min.» and «Sec.» with note numbers. «Numerus dicrum», «Numerus horarum» and «Partes3) horarum» are printed turned through a quarter, reading upwards, in two lines; here their words stand in L03 and L04. Each printed row is one line here, the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The hours end with 24 (L29).",
  "L06-L35. Checked against the daily mean motion of Jupiter of Tab. 11 (p. 122, JP2 0154), 4′ 59″ 9‴ with Brahmagupta's parameter: the 30 days agree with n × 4′ 59.15″ to within 0.5″ (with the readings of notes a and b), and the 24 hours with n × 12.46″ to within 0.5″ (with the readings of notes c-e). The «partes horarum», the sixtieths of an hour, are counted at 12″ to the hour, a fifth of a second to the part, rounded to the second (2 to 60 parts: 0 to 12 seconds; with the reading of note f): all as printed.",
  "L04 and N01: «dicrum» and «Dakaicac»; see the critical notes. N02: «V. notas in tab. 8.», in italics; N04: «in ras.», in italics, the reading of C written over an erasure. The «—» after «C 49v» in the margin note is a long dash, set close."
